  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, the triangle formed by a line parallel to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the straight line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is shown below.<br /><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0028_46d13ae7aa2f.jpg\" style=\"width: 316px; height: 286px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br />Since, area of <math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>ABC</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>h</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mtext>AB</mtext> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mtext>AC</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>h</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Where <math> <mrow> <mtext>AB</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>AC</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&#183;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup><mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>h</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>h</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>h</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>&#177;</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>k</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Hence, the locus of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>&#177;</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>y</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>"
